### Modifications

The sprite is not byte-identical to the upstream file. Changes made here, as
required by the Apache License 2.0, section 4(b):

- **`information` trimmed.** The upstream symbol repeats its dial and its bar as
  two extra `fill="currentColor"` paths on top of a path that already draws both.
  Those two paths are removed so the glyph is a single shape; the drawn result is
  unchanged.
- **Brand mark replaced.** The retired `kubesphere` glyph is removed, and
  `kubeaihub` now draws the Kube AI Hub mark: a solid hexagon with three connected
  nodes carved out of it. The cut-outs are sub-paths of a single `fill-rule="evenodd"`
  path rather than a `mask`, so the glyph carries no id reference and survives being
  inlined more than once on a page.
- **Duplicate paint paths removed.** Where a symbol ends with a path that repaints,
  in the same ink, a shape an earlier `fill-rule="evenodd"` path already carved
  out, the repaint is dropped and the cut-out shows again. Without this the mark
  and its plate merged into one solid mass — `logout-right-duotone`,
  `login-left-duotone`, `tags-duotone` and `switch-button-duotone` all rendered
  as blobs. `switch-button-duotone` also gains an explicit `.22` track plate so
  its knobs still separate from the rails.
- **White detail fills made transparent.** Twelve symbols painted inner detail in
  a hard-coded `#FFF`/`white` (`golang`, `client`, `cron-job`, `deamon-set`,
  `gateway`, `job`, `springcloud`, `ssd`, `vsan`, `edge`, `crane`,
  `up-circle-duotone`). That detail is invisible on a light surface and wrong on
  any tinted one. Those fills are now `none`, so the surface behind the glyph
  shows through, which is what the artwork intended. `mask` and `clipPath`
  geometry keeps its white: it is not ink.
- **Fixed-palette fills replaced with `currentColor`.** Upstream hard-codes a
  light grey (`#CCD3DB`, `#B6C2CD`), a dark navy (`#36435C`, `#242E42`,
  `#C1C9D1`, `#14215A`) and an off-white (`#F9FBFD`) as secondary or cut-out
  fills. Those values only read correctly on one surface tone, so on a dark theme
  the light greys sank into the background and on a light theme the cut-outs
  disappeared. They are now `currentColor` with `fill-opacity`, which follows the
  surrounding text colour and stays legible on every theme. The drawn shapes are
  unchanged; only how they take their colour changed.
- **Everything else is unmodified.** Apart from the brand mark and the colour
  substitution above, the remaining symbols are byte-identical to upstream, in the
  same order. `timed-task`, `clock`, `calendar` and `history-duotone` are among them.

Upstream duplicate ids (`barchart`, `springcloud`, `stretch`, `event` each appear
twice) are reproduced as-is. They are an upstream quirk rather than a change made
here: `ICON_NAMES` lists each id once because a browser resolves `<use>` to the
last definition, so the duplicate is unreachable.

Three symbols are not well-formed in upstream and are left that way rather than
guessed at, because no rendering of them is known to be correct: `springcloud`
and `springcloudgateway` contain unbalanced `<g>` elements, and
`download-box-2-duotone` closes with a bare `<symbol>` instead of `</symbol>`.
A bare `<symbol>` opener appears ten times upstream and swallows whatever follows
it, so these glyphs may fail to render; fixing them needs the original artwork,
not a repair of the markup alone.

